# APEX API keys template (placeholders only, no real secrets in this file)
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Do NOT fill in this file. Copy it to a private location OUTSIDE any
#      Google Drive synced folder and OUTSIDE the APEX project tree:
#         mkdir -p ~/.apex && cp "APEX_API_KEYS_TEMPLATE.env.example" ~/.apex/.env && chmod 600 ~/.apex/.env
#   2. Edit ~/.apex/.env and paste keys there.
#   3. Never paste keys into the collaboration doc, Drive, email or chat.
#
# RULES
#   - Testnet / paper-only keys. No withdrawal or transfer permission.
#   - Trade permission only if a paper-order task is explicitly scoped; read-only otherwise.
#   - Public funding and market data (Deribit, Kraken) needs NO keys. Leave blank.
#   - Revoke and rotate any key that is ever pasted somewhere shared.
#   - Stage 2 frozen files and manifest must not be edited; keep this file outside that tree.
#
# NOTE: the current APEX code does not read these variable names yet.
# ChatGPT should define the final names when the paper-order task is scoped;
# rename the entries below to match.

# --- Deribit TESTNET (test.deribit.com) ---
DERIBIT_TESTNET_CLIENT_ID=
DERIBIT_TESTNET_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Kraken Futures DEMO (demo-futures.kraken.com) ---
KRAKEN_DEMO_API_KEY=
KRAKEN_DEMO_API_SECRET=

# --- Optional: ALFRED / FRED (point-in-time macro vintages; free key, read-only) ---
FRED_API_KEY=

# --- Mode guard: keep "shadow" until paper-order routing is approved ---
APEX_EXECUTION_MODE=shadow
